; test clifpeep
; `x >s -1` with x = uextend (i8) in [0, 255]: always true. Narrow
; `iconst.i32 -1` is stored zero-extended (0xffffffff), and the vmax
; signed rules compared that raw value against x's ceiling (`k >= mx`
; -> fold false): bevy_math's IRect::union_point kept the point's
; negative y as the max (rect_union_pt). Signed rules must see k
; sign-extended.
; check: iconst.i8 1
; check-not: iconst.i8 0
; diffcheck
function %sgt(i8) -> i8 fast {
block0(v0: i8):
    v1 = uextend.i32 v0
    v2 = iconst.i32 -1
    v3 = icmp sgt v1, v2
    return v3
}
